LU: Trie_Max Xor Subarray
Success rate: 58.33%

Given an array arr[] of size N, find the subarray with the maximum XOR. A subarray is a contiguous part of the array.

Input Format:
The first line contains an integer N representing the size of the array.
The second line contains N space-separated integers representing the elements of the array.

Output Format:
Output a single integer, the maximum XOR value of any subarray.

Constraints:
1 <= N <= 10^5
1 <= arr[i] <= 10^5

Sample test cases
Input
15
1 2 3 4 5 6 7 87 19 100 11 23 45 67 12
Expected output

126

